From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Static Everywhere <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SDL: explicitly show the window after backend initialization

SDL normally maps a window unless SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN is requested, but some
X11 implementations defer the initial map while the renderer/context is being
constructed.  Publish the window explicitly after backend initialization so
the visible startup contract does not depend on that timing detail.

---
 WinPort/src/Backend/SDL/SDLMain.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/WinPort/src/Backend/SDL/SDLMain.cpp b/WinPort/src/Backend/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
index efcdfadf..98be5704 100644
--- a/WinPort/src/Backend/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
+++ b/WinPort/src/Backend/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
@@ -2552,6 +2552,11 @@ bool SDLConsoleApp::Initialize()
 	}
 
 	_backend->Attach();
+	// SDL_CreateWindow normally maps a window unless SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN is
+	// requested.  Publish it explicitly after backend initialization as well:
+	// this keeps startup deterministic on X11 implementations that defer the
+	// initial map while the renderer/context is being constructed.
+	SDL_ShowWindow(_window);
 
 	if (win_state.valid) {
 		if (win_state.fullscreen) {
